 more than half a second, and remained unchallenged in the second descent. The silver medal went to Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/110427"} "Shelley Rudman"] ", which was something of an upset. Rudman had started competing in skeleton after watching " [:a {:href "/athletes/101684"} "Alex Coomber"] " winning a bronze in 2002, but had not been named for a top position in Torino. She edged out " [:a {:href "/athletes/110426"} "Mellisa Hollingsworth-Richards"] ", winner of that season’s World Cup and 2004 World Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/101685"} "Diane Sartor"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Run #1"] [:th {} "Run #2"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/101686"} "Maya Pedersen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} "1:59.83"] [:td {} "59.64 (1)"] [:td {} "1:00.19 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/110427"} "Shelley Rudman"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "2:01.06"] [:td {} "1:00.57 (4)"] [:td {} "1:00.49 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/110426"} "Mellisa Hollingsworth-Richards"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "2:01.41"] [:td {} "1:00.39 (3)"] [:td {} "1:01.02 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td 